// AUTO-GENERATED — do not hand-edit. Regenerate from the ^GSPC daily history.
// See "md files/CHANGELOG.md" (2026-08-24).
//
// SOURCE: S&P 500 cash index (^GSPC) daily closes, 1927-12-30 -> 2026-08-21,
// 24,777 sessions. Price return only — dividends excluded.
// The VIX study additionally uses ^VIX and ^GSPC daily OHLC from Yahoo,
// 1990-01-02 -> 2026-08-21 (9,227 joined sessions) — VIX does not exist before.
//
// SEASONAL_BASELINES — for each window, the average cumulative % path across
// its years. Each year is re-based to its own prior 31-Dec close, laid on a
// 365-day calendar axis (29-Feb dropped), forward-filled across weekends and
// holidays, then averaged. Index 0 = Jan 1, index 364 = Dec 31.
//
// YEAR_CURVES — the same construction, per individual year, for the overlay
// picker. Stored as a comma-joined string of INTEGER HUNDREDTHS OF A PERCENT
// and parsed on first use, not at module load: 98 years x 365 points is the
// single biggest thing in this file, and the overwhelming majority of visitors
// never open the picker. Do not "simplify" this into a number[][] literal —
// that is ~2.5x the bytes and it parses for everyone.
//
// It lives in the JS bundle rather than a fetched /public/*.json ON PURPOSE.
// The middleware matcher excludes ".js" but its "js(?!on)" lookahead does NOT
// exclude ".json", so a fetched year file would be auth-gated and 307 to "/"
// for exactly the signed-out visitors /explore/seasonality exists to serve.
//
// YTD_2026_* — the live year on the same construction: cumulative % from the
// 2025 close (6845.50) and the raw index close, index 0 = Jan 1.
//
// ALMANAC / EXTRAS — the tables. Monthly and annual aggregates exclude the
// current partial year and the final partial month.

export type SeasonalBaseline = {
  key: string;
  label: string;
  /** Year span the average covers, for the caption. */
  span: string;
  /** How many years went into the average. */
  years: number;
  /** 365 values, cumulative % from the prior year-end. */
  curve: number[];
};

